A||||8||malacite||Brake Upgrade...Drilled or Slotted?||||1||
Z||000000||malacite||12-13-2001||12:52 AM||||Here's the deal...i want new rotors for the front of my saturn. my choices are cross drilled discs ($99.99) or Slotted discs ($99.99)<P>i plan on autocrossing, and possibly scca Rallycross<P>------------------<BR>Malacite<P>Grendel-88 Fiero RIP<BR>'94 Saturn SW2 RallySport<BR>'95 Saturn SL1 Touring||||reg||1
Z||000001||DKOV||12-13-2001||01:41 AM||||Whoa... Somehow I was transported to the Saturn Forum?!??!  Freaky!<P>Drilled OR crossed?  I don't get it... why not BOTH!!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>DKOV -||||reg||1
Z||000002||malacite||12-13-2001||02:17 AM||||yeah...well actually no.<P>i'm an old fiero guy who's fiero decided it was tired and wanted to sleep. so she dropped me off into a saturn. and ran off with an older mechanic with a spare 3800.<P>but you guys are a wealth of knowledge and i couldn't bring myself to do somthing like this without opinions.<P>besides. brakes are brakes, no matter what car you have. the upgrade should have the same effect on any car. right?||||reg||12
Z||000003||fieroman_5000||12-13-2001||12:03 PM||||By slotted do you mean vented by any chance?? if so I'd go wwith the vented. just my .02<P>Fieroman <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000004||Ali_Gulf_Fiero||12-13-2001||01:44 PM||||I agree with Fieroman - vented.<BR>Better fade resistance without loss of swept area.<BR><P>------------------<BR>my cat's sitting in my scrambled eggs.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Wannabe||12-13-2001||03:49 PM||||Don't confuse slotted with vented. Vented means there is a space between the friction surfaces of the rotor that allows air to pass between and cool the rotor. Unless you need to lok good, don't concern yourself with slotted or drilled rotors. Stick with a good quality OEM or OEM replacement nad get yourself the best street/race pad you can afford. Also make sure your brakes are working properly to begin with.||||reg||1
Z||000006||BlackARROW||12-13-2001||05:58 PM||||I've heard that the drilled disks tend more to wave on hard&hot usage than the vented one (slotted?). Probably it is not the case with drilled Carbon disk.. but probably more than 99$  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Since you are going to race with it, it may be something to think of.<P><P>------------------<BR>BlackARROW &gt;&gt;--&gt;<BR>Gadgeteered Fiero 2M4 '85<BR>"Get your groove on"||||reg||1
Z||000007||artherd||12-14-2001||03:18 AM|||| <A HREF="http://www.movit.de/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.movit.de/</A> <P>BIG SLOPPY GRIN!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Seriously though, neither drilling or slotting will actually gain you any real performance.  Grab a set of Teflon/SS lines, and change the fluid to a good Full Synthetic DOT4 (ATE SuperBlue rocks) and get some aggressive pads.<P>You'll actually notice a change !  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>PS: Yes, I have drilled rotors on my Ttop formula, they're just for looks I assure you!<P>Full system restoration/rebuild with SS lines, carbomnet pads, and ATE fluid, and the  damned shoddy Fiero system still won't lock the wheels when hot... (It will when cold, after about a second...)  I'm throwing Big Reds on there (porsche 993 TT GT2 brakes)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000008||fieroman_5000||12-14-2001||07:55 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Ali_Gulf_Fiero:<BR><B>I agree with Fieroman - vented.<BR>Better fade resistance without loss of swept area.<P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>thanx Gulf_Fiero. I was just thinking that drilled were only for looks aswell. I like those vented <B>and</B> drilled rotors on that posted website  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>Fieroman <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>||||reg||1
